## Why This Is Asked
Real-time analytics require fast percentile queries with inserts/deletes while handling duplicates.

## Key Concepts
- Coordinate compression maps latencies to a compact domain.
- Fenwick tree maintains prefix counts efficiently.
- kth-order statistic via binary lifting yields the percentile value.
- Carefully handle erase when a value count reaches zero.

## Code Example
```javascript
class Fenwick {
  constructor(n){ this.n=n; this.bit=new Array(n+1).fill(0); }
  update(i, delta){ for(; i<=this.n; i+= i&-i) this.bit[i]+=delta; }
  query(i){ let s=0; for(; i>0; i-= i&-i) s+=this.bit[i]; return s; }
  kth(k){ let idx=0; let bit=1; while((bit<<1) <= this.n) bit<<=1; for(; bit>0; bit>>=1){ let nxt = idx + bit; if(nxt <= this.n && this.bit[nxt] < k){ idx = nxt; k -= this.bit[nxt]; } } return idx+1; }
}
```

